      "title": "Truist Financial Explores AFCO Credit Sale to Sharpen Strategic Focus",
      "summary": "Truist Financial is exploring the potential sale of AFCO Credit Corp., its insurance premium financing business with $6-7 billion in assets, as part of efforts to streamline operations and focus on core banking. This follows the bank's $5.5 billion near-prime auto loan exit and planned $7.7 billion LightStream divestiture to Carlyle Group. The moves aim to improve funding efficiency and profitability, though sale terms remain uncertain.",
