      "title": "TFC Q3 Earnings Miss Estimates as Securities Losses, Higher Costs Hurt",
      "summary": "Truist Financial's Q3 2026 adjusted EPS rose 11.5% year-over-year to $1.16 but missed consensus estimates by one cent due to $1.4 billion in securities losses and higher non-interest expenses. The company benefited from record wealth management income and 3.6% deposit growth, but profitability metrics weakened significantly. Management projects Q4 revenues of $5.35B with NII of $3.65-$3.70B.",
